<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Response&nbsp;--&gt;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">&lt;--&nbsp;Thanks&nbsp;for&nbsp;critting!&nbsp;:)</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Hey gee0765,</p>
<p>Firstly, thanks for reading my article through and giving me some feedback, it's all very useful in the process of writing this story.</p>
<p>To address some of the critique you've provided in your feedback, I totally agree with the second description being a little counter-intuitive and confused and will touch that up on a future update to the current article to make it less so.</p>
<p>Furthermore, I disagree with your first criticism about the initial four logs from the doctor, they serve to explain the history of the item in question.</p>
<p>The exploration logs are an exploration of the object's anomalous effects and also give us a little exploration of our four characters who have been sent in, alone, to deal with something that the Foundation doesn't even understand, but I do agree in part with the crit concerning them blending together in their current state. I think that is a problem that I'll go over and hopefully fix.</p>
<p>Finally, the reveal at the end isn't the existence of the creature, but the fact that it's containment procedure is failing. The lance that's got it impaled is slowly deteriorating, that's why the fragments were snapping off so easily as well. The Foundation is on limited time and it's only so long before the creature is freed.</p>
<p>As to the compulsion effects, it's not compulsion to the same degree as many other cosmic entities &quot;forcing&quot; their subjects to work towards them but rather that humans are being utilised and played with like human toys. The entity is a child-like being that's grasping out with its &quot;hands&quot; and that's what's twisting reality around them.</p>
<p>However, having said all this, I do agree that it could do with a rewrite to better clarify these intended outcomes and messages.</p>
<p>Overall, thank you very much for the critique!</p>
</div>
