			<div class="content" id="post-content-4476800">
									

<p>Personal nitpick, I don't enjoy it when a fairly well know piece of media, in this case, the pretty specific depiction of the Lance of Longinus from NGE, is lifted and re-used without some in universe reasoning. Feels to me a bit too much like pandering, and at worst, theft.</p>
<p>There were mysteries here that I wanted to know more about, if you are open to doing any substantial editing after the contest is over. I think the story could benefit from exploring, maybe just in hints, without spelling it out too quickly, some things like: why the carvings on the lance feature imagery whose sources (the creatures in evolutionary line, for example) did not exist at the time of the object's creation; whther the age of the lance, or the time of its arrival on earth are significant; why the entity is contained on earth, or why it happened to be on earth when it was contained (other than the fact that otherwise there wouldn't be a story); how Higgs' interactions with the entity or the lance might have contribited to the lance's deterioration (something to justify his appearance at the end as more than a creepypasta trope). The image of a powerful entity, in unstable containment is a really compelling one, which I'm sure is why there are so many examples of exactly that on this site. I just think this one needs more flavor to differentiate it from the others.</p>

